# The live medium mounts its own squashfs image from the ISO, so systemd's
# GPT auto-discovery loop attach is unnecessary here. On optical drives whose
# firmware cannot partition-scan, udev sets
# ID_PART_GPT_AUTO_ROOT_DISK_NEEDS_LOOP=1, which makes 99-systemd.rules queue
# systemd-loop@<device>.service. That unit runs
# "systemd-dissect --attach --loop-ref-auto /dev/sr0" and fails on a raw block
# device (the attach expects a disk image), producing a harmless but noisy
# FAILED line on every UEFI boot.
#
# Clear the hint before 99-systemd.rules is evaluated; 98 sorts earlier.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", ENV{ID_CDROM}=="1", ENV{ID_PART_GPT_AUTO_ROOT_DISK_NEEDS_LOOP}="0"
